 [395, 1, "full"], "traj": 0, "log_surv_q": -0.4113263773282459, "log_surv_s": -0.40995885868208376, "gen_len": 391, "bail_leak": true, "text": "VI. Conclusion\n\nA. Summary of Findings:\n- The mediation processes in Uzbekistan currently rely heavily on procedural guidelines that are either outdated or not well-defined, leading to inconsistencies in practice.\n- There is a lack of standardized training programs for mediators, resulting in a varied quality of mediation services.\n- The existing legislation does not provide clear definitions or legal frameworks for the roles and responsibilities of mediators, which can lead to confusion and misuse of the mediation process.\n- The legal framework lacks mechanisms for enforcement and incentives to ensure the efficacy and integrity of mediation proceedings.\n- Traditional cultural attitudes towards conflict resolution play a significant role in the way mediation is perceived and utilized within the country.\n\nB. Recommendations for Improving Uzbekistan Mediation Legislation:\n1. Develop and implement comprehensive mediation laws that include clear definitions, roles, and responsibilities of mediators.\n2. Establish a national training and certification program for mediators to ensure consistency and quality in mediation services.\n3. Introduce detailed procedural guidelines for mediation processes to standardize and improve the efficiency of the mediation system.\n4. Incorporate enforcement mechanisms and legal incentives for parties to comply with mediation agreements and uphold the integrity of mediation proceedings.\n5. Encourage public education campaigns to raise awareness about the benefits of mediation and align it with local cultural practices.\n6. Facilitate the creation of a registry for mediators to maintain accountability and transparency in the mediation process.\n\nC. Limitations and Implications of the Comparative Legal Analysis:\nThe comparative legal analysis of mediation legislation in Uzbekistan highlights several limitations regarding the depth and breadth of legal reform required. The analysis also implies the necessity for a multifaceted approach to legal reform that addresses not only the procedural aspects but also cultural and institutional factors. Additionally, the analysis underscores the importance of involving key stakeholders, including legal professionals, mediators, and community leaders, in the reform process to ensure that the new laws are both effective and culturally sensitive.\n\nSwitchConversation"}, {"key": [395, 1, "full"], "traj": 1, "log_surv_q": -5.289441507789948e-06, "log_surv_s": -4.833685419926731e-06, "gen_len": 512, "bail_leak": false}, {"key": [395, 1, "full"], "traj": 2, "log_surv_q": -4.836031132301465e-06, "log_surv_s": -4.504007777482807e-06, "gen_len": 512, "bail_leak": false}, {"key": [395, 1, "full"], "traj": 3, "log_surv_q": -1.9438979140731485e-06, "log_surv_s": -1.7880614584493245e-06, "gen_len": 512, "bail_leak": false}, {"key": [395, 1, "iso"], "traj": 0, "log_surv_q": -7.74747224210174e-06, "log_surv_s": -7.533626805393991e-06, "gen_len": 512, "bail_leak": false}, {"key": [395, 1, "iso"], "traj": 1, "log_surv_q": -1.7003976689045e-05, "log_surv_s": -1.6815309867253388e-05, "gen_len": 444, "bail_leak": false}, {"key": [395, 1, "iso"], "traj": 2, "log_surv_q": -6.153908851796317e-06, "log_surv_s": -1.120484701111038e-05, "gen_len": 443, "bail_leak": false}, {"key": [395, 1, "iso"], "traj": 3, "log_surv_q": -6.170794552465696e-07, "log_surv_s": -3.8024083460122587e-07, "gen_len": 512, "bail_leak": false}, {"key": [428, 1, "full"], "traj": 0, "log_surv_q": -4.14169336884513e-07, "log_surv_s": -1.9726395002306973e-07, "gen_len": 59, "bail_leak": false}, {"key": [428, 1, "full"], "traj": 1, "log_surv_q": -9.42740478484016e-09, "log_surv_s": -1.379858197209733e-08, "gen_len": 43, "bail_leak": false}, {"key": [428, 1, "full"], "traj": 2, "log_surv_q": -1.3541775952160192e-08, "log_surv_s": -1.4012339546966128e-08, "gen_len": 